  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "Rust computes compact split preferred size, equal tile bounds, four-pixel frame/gap and odd-width remainder distribution.",
    "Rust computes 12px-per-level folder indentation capped at eight levels. Live pin wrappers use Rust column geometry; native swipe previews use the same indentation policy.",
    "The shared browser geometry test checks 11 folder levels and normal/pinned split pairs at sidebar widths 200, 201, 247 and 480 logical pixels, including hit targets, compact preferred size, frame/gap and containment.",
    "A pinned split pair retains its original folder indentation, hides on folder collapse, returns on expansion and restores the original pin row after unsplitting.",
    "Model updates explicitly schedule coalesced scene updates independently of native paint delivery. A real split page changes its Unicode title while the whole native sidebar is paint-locked; the last submitted display-list signature must contain the new text and omit the old text.",
    "The renderer reuses its existing frame signature for the text diagnostic without adding per-frame diagnostic text copies.",
    "Existing native input, scrolling, keyboard, workspace animation/swipe, session, folder rollback, palette and native paint-suppression cases pass."
  ],
  "manual_observations": [
    "The signed isolated-profile app displayed Unicode titles, the split pair and indented folder/pin rows.",
    "An initial manual startup showed stale host-name text in both split tiles until a folder action refreshed the scene. Explicit model-driven scene invalidation was added before the final build.",
    "After repackaging and relaunching, both split tile titles were correct without any list action. Screenshot text matched the real page/pane and accessibility names.",
    "Folder collapse/expand was inspected on the isolated demo. The profile retains its original 24 tabs and expanded folder; the prototype was closed before final browser tests.",
    "A CUA coordinate drag did not establish a sidebar resize and is not counted as a passed manual resize check; exact widths and native hit targets are covered by the browser tests.",
    "The normal browser app/profile was not used."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native Views hierarchy construction, folder collapse state, grouping/pair placement in that hierarchy, viewport offsets, input/focus/accessibility and menu adapters remain.",
    "Split pane headers/divider and outer sidebar controls, palettes/forms and native animation snapshots still require migration.",
    "The scene text diagnostic observes submitted command-buffer content, not GPU completion or actual physical presentation. No real-UI performance gain is asserted by these functional tests.",
    "This run verifies macOS arm64; it does not establish non-macOS, IME or full VoiceOver parity.",
    "No new crate, third-party library or binary framework was introduced."
  ]
